  conflictPresets:
  - '[FactionA] and [FactionB] left the contested lands in ruins after days of brutal
    fighting.'
  - The struggle for the territory between [FactionA] and [FactionB] has ended, leaving
    both sides battered.
  - '[FactionA] claims victory over [FactionB] in the recently fought-over lands.'
  - The battle for the land between [FactionA] and [FactionB] is over, but the wounds
    of war remain.
  alliancePresets:
  - '[FactionA] and [FactionB] have signed a mutual defense pact, vowing to stand
    together against future threats.'
  - Diplomatic talks conclude with [FactionA] and [FactionB] officially forming an
    alliance.
  - In a rare show of unity, [FactionA] and [FactionB] join forces to face a common
    enemy.
  - Former rivals [FactionA] and [FactionB] have set aside past grievances to unite
    under one banner.
  brokenAlliancePresets:
  - '[FactionA] and [FactionB] have officially dissolved their alliance after growing
    tensions.'
  - Once close allies, [FactionA] and [FactionB] part ways, citing irreconcilable
    differences.
  - '[FactionB] accuses [FactionA] of betrayal, ending their long-standing partnership.'
  - Diplomatic ties between [FactionA] and [FactionB] collapse, marking the end of
    their alliance.
  relationshipsForming:
  - "[FactionA]\u2019s assault on a mutual enemy has brought [FactionB] closer, strengthening
    their alliance."
  - By striking a common foe, [FactionA] and [FactionB] find their ties growing stronger.
  - "[FactionB] praises [FactionA]\u2019s recent attack on their hated rival, boosting
    mutual trust."
  - Shared hostility toward [FactionC] deepens the bond between [FactionA] and [FactionB].
  relationshipsFalling:
  - "[FactionA]\u2019s recent aggression has strained ties with [FactionB], causing
    a rift."
  - Relations between [FactionA] and [FactionB] sour following unexpected hostilities.
  - "[FactionB] condemns [FactionA]\u2019s actions, marking a downturn in their relationship."
  - '[FactionA] risks alienation as tensions with [FactionB] continue to rise.'
  temporaryAlliancePresets:
  - '[FactionA] and [FactionB] have formed a temporary alliance to face a greater
    threat.'
  - In a cautious move, [FactionA] and [FactionB] set aside differences for a limited
    partnership.
  - Temporary truce declared as [FactionA] and [FactionB] unite against a common
    enemy.
  - '[FactionB] and [FactionA] agree to a short-term alliance amid rising hostilities.'
  brokenTemporaryAlliancePresets:
  - '[FactionA] and [FactionB] have ended their temporary alliance following the
    resolution of the common threat.'
  - With the danger passed, [FactionA] and [FactionB] dissolve their short-term partnership.
  - The temporary truce between [FactionA] and [FactionB] has expired as the shared
    enemy is defeated.
  - '[FactionB] and [FactionA] part ways after successfully overcoming the immediate
    threat.'
  factionColors:
  - {r: 0.20392159, g: 0.52156866, b: 0.6156863, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.5018867, g: 0.1543538, b: 0.18942606, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.7283019, g: 0.4780441, b: 0.19650406, a: 1}
  - {r: 0.3921569, g: 0.4901961, b: 0.20392159, a: 1}
  replaceFactionA: '[FactionA]'
  replaceFactionB: '[FactionB]'
